{"title":"2024 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 2 Part C","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2\" title=\"2024 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2_Part_C&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/d/64d5bf9467bb99266c7eacee768975dc69fd5844.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{1} = -6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/f/52f74c62b890e5b3b0ce552416aabffd78f5fc71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_{1} = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/3/04348d1931c4f561d045ee5264831388d88d02f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_{1} = -5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"17\" />. For each positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/72287b09043ed45b372a517d764e12d07aff8071.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, let\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b64c9d4323a1fb8b84398adc4b74ced09ad3e79a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{n} = 2B_{n - 1} - (A_{n - 1})^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"181\" height=\"21\" /></center>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/f/fefa7e630a0c92bf503e3eb8b1d3430134243d7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_{n} = (B_{n - 1})^{2} - 2A_{n - 1}C_{n - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"220\" height=\"21\" /></center>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/b/bdb8e42132dbf4ade0484d84739763e689a00e91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_{n} = -(C_{n - 1})^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"123\" height=\"21\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2_Part_C&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can suppose that the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/0/6e0c04ac8fe0755031f7661088033e207b944e83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_{n}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> has roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> (which are not necessarily distinct). Using vieta's or multiplying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/2/c6226ea5ed2be03c1581921e50d490381044f0c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x - r)(x - s)(x - t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"20\" /> out, we see:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/4/06470d557c8130b74f33bacb376bd4f4e9ed49d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-(r + s + t) = A_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"145\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/e/9fea63db9f3ad54a13dc08f68bf9ace4f8588f0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$rs + rt + st = B_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/2/c425143be8e5033c4f4b4af794447ef271c68701.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-rst = C_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>We can then consider the first polynomial, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/e/11ef5766b0426af45297faae19e02b472a57a59b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_{1}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" />, where:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/f/93f8aa4e419aaa19603ddfd602bdc59c4d0319dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_{1}(x) = x^{3} - 6x^{2} + 10x - 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"216\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>By inspection, we see that we can factor out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/c/49c5a98b61f4aab3a68ef6ccc3a3faf7dc170807.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/e/02e8821769d050766c635a4d78958e14da56d016.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_{1}(1) = 1 - 6 + 10 - 5 = -5 + 5 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"290\" height=\"20\" />. This gives:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/f/08f1fb154683335f514862eddabbc0e8dbf13e37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_{1}(x) = (x - 1)(x^{5} - 5x + 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"228\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>We can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/c/d5c216432b00f6bff9fdd38d91d182593d7d8516.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{5} - 5x + 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" /> has a discriminant of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/b/80b2b0bd38cafb04ce97a3f2837438316d41a108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{2} - 5 \\times 4 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" />. The square root of this is less than the value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/4/8f482fd254bc8b4cc5b527d9a093a090c9096908.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-(-5) = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"87\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/a/86a14ba730789020c293925a0aa3da63f92f76b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />, meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/c/d5c216432b00f6bff9fdd38d91d182593d7d8516.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{5} - 5x + 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" /> must have two distinct positive real roots.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/e/11ef5766b0426af45297faae19e02b472a57a59b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_{1}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" /> must have three distinct positive real roots.\n</p><p>Next, we can assume it's true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/0/6e0c04ac8fe0755031f7661088033e207b944e83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_{n}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/72287b09043ed45b372a517d764e12d07aff8071.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />. Using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/6/d963f7e97b1b154eb96a0b817b54a4ddaae07d22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{n - 1} = -(r + s + t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"162\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/2/9525bd658b8da088781785029553ede024b77b56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_{n - 1} = rs + rt + st$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/d/2ed0f504aba1a0270cc3931be459b4ec5571a2b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_{n - 1} = -rst$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" />, and the definitions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/5/d555a2fb62bf338fd13e9d9ced457fe49932324e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/0/610bb8d6a25ceeb883b9231cdd91040b0edd4b3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/6/fe6f3297e10caab75fced16e89490a59895e80da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/0/06060294dcbc617a08ebc9a792a964d198f21e53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{n} = 2(rs + rt + st) - (-(r + s + t))^{2} = 2(rs + rt + st) - (r^{2} + s^{2} + t^{2} + 2(rs + rt + st))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"708\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/e/ccece3e44e71f05d9e81f216f61a78b710103c3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{n}=-(r^{2} + s^{2} + t^{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"168\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87e6517bd85d78623354209a771fe590891db313.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_{n} = (rs + rt + st)^{2} - 2(-(r + s + t) \\times - rst) = r^{2}s^{2} + r^{2}t^{2} + s^{2}t^{2} + 2(rs \\times rt + rs \\times st + rt \\times st) - 2(r^{2}st + rs^{2}t + rst^{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"961\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78704a7fe8a2d1081f55006374d7c7849bf51e66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=r^{2}s^{2} + r^{2}t^{2} + s^{2}t^{2} + 2r^{2}st + 2rs^{2}t + 2rst^{2} - 2r^{2}st - 2rs^{2}t - 2rst^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"533\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/6/016a96ae2fa794e54f0430851bdda0523e2fd301.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_{n}=r^{2}s^{2} + r^{2}t^{2} + s^{2}t^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"186\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/9/73957819bd6bbd6ce365e3d80ba78f7e7e6a3a62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_{n} = -(-rst)^{2} = -r^{2}s^{2}t^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"206\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>This means that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/7/d072a8de3e3f00d5b79837561d1964400ae935cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_{n}(x) = x^{3} - (r^{2} + s^{2} + t^{2})x^{2} + (r^{2}s^{2} + r^{s}t^{2} + s^{2}t^{2})x - (r^{2}s^{2}t^{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"497\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>From this, we can realise that the roots of the polynomial are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/2/fe2824044830deac407616cba3b764d79e50137b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^{2}$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/b/f7b59ba357a1b54473c0c4dbe8672bb404f04770.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s^{2}$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/0/dd047a1d2223b15a6faef36abb36f26a71b1a50f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" />. This means that the roots of the next equation would just be the square of the roots of the previous equation.\n</p><p>Thus, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/e/11ef5766b0426af45297faae19e02b472a57a59b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_{1}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" /> has three distinct positive real roots, the square of the roots will always be different positive numbers for each subsequent value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/3/723d8c0f4846a293f09776078bbbdb232ba27087.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_{2}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/a/93a186e554447950477d4bbaa08dc38385598e40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_{3}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"43\" height=\"20\" />, etc will also have three distinct positive real roots.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/8/e78c570c393090f53c72a03d27ab97d03ee5fa96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_{100}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> must have three distinct positive real roots.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2_Part_C&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>This problem needs a solution. If you have a solution for it, please help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2_Part_C&amp;action=edit\">adding it</a></span>.</i> \n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018065759\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.048 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 264/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 546/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9467/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   21.538      1 -total\n 29.44%    6.341      1 Template:Solution\n 27.44%    5.910      1 2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37463:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018065759 and revision id 289499. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}